# The four rtnetlink dumps (RTM_GETLINK, RTM_GETADDR, RTM_GETROUTE and RTM_GETNEXTHOP, each for AF_UNSPEC)
# of one network namespace, as Linux 6.8.0 (aarch64, so little-endian) answered them: one netlink
# message per line, its header included, in hex, after the name of its dump. refused.ip-link.json
# (ip -d -j link show) and refused.ip-addr.json (ip -j addr show) are iproute2's reading of the same
# namespace at the same moment. links_linux_test.go says how the namespace was built.
